inix-build → nix build

Old command: nix-build

This command was used to build Nix expressions or derivations, typically specified via a default.nix file or a package expression.

New command: nix build

In flakes, the nix build command is used to build the outputs specified in a flake.nix. Flakes introduce a more structured approach, where flake.nix defines inputs and outputs.






nix-collect-garbage → nix flake prune

Old command: nix-collect-garbage

This command was used to remove unused Nix store paths, freeing up disk space.

New command: nix flake prune

The flake command nix flake prune is more specific to cleaning up unused flake-based packages, builds, and outputs.


nix-env → nix profile

Old command: nix-env

The nix-env command was traditionally used to manage user profiles, installing, upgrading, or removing packages.

New command: nix profile

Flakes have introduced the nix profile command for managing user environments in a more reproducible way. This new command allows for installing, upgrading, and switching profiles defined by flakes.

